# Feature module conventions

Each feature is self-contained under `src/features/<name>/`:

```
api/         data access (TanStack Query hooks, fetchers), schemas.ts (zod)
components/  feature-local presentational components
hooks/       feature-local hooks
screens/     screen containers (own data + orchestration)
types/       feature types
index.ts     PUBLIC surface — the only thing other features may import
```

- **Import boundaries:** other features import only from this feature's `index.ts`. Inside the feature, use relative or `@/features/<name>/...` paths.
- **Container vs presentational:** screens own data hooks and navigation; extract layout into pure, typed components. Split a screen when it exceeds ~200 lines or mixes fetching with heavy layout.
- **Copy is i18n:** never hard-code user-facing strings — add keys to `src/translations/en-EN.json` and use `useTranslation()`.
- **Validation:** define zod schemas in `api/schemas.ts`; validate at API boundaries and surface field errors in inputs.
- **Navigation:** use route names/params from `src/navigation/paths.ts` + `types.ts`, not string literals.
